# Byte-exact checkout. No EOL conversion in either direction.
#
# Why: docs/sha256.txt tells readers they can verify this repository against a
# md5 baseline. With autocrlf on, a fresh clone on Windows would rewrite every
# LF to CRLF and every hash would differ. Reproducibility beats local comfort
# here, so all files are stored and checked out exactly as committed.
* -text

# These three are still recognised as text for tooling that asks git for type
# information (diff, merge), but without any conversion.
*.md    diff
*.py    diff
*.json  diff

# Windows-only launcher; keep it executable-cross-platform irrelevant but marked
*.ps1   diff
